Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:04:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 140/144] GreatDANE: prefer the ESR Preprocessor and mirror
 installer.nsi pre-branding defines (round 4k)

Parse module.ver with mozbuild.preprocessor.Preprocessor(marker='%') from
the Firefox ESR 153.7.0 tree when it is importable, falling back to the
minimal %define/%include reimplementation. Pre-define MOZ_APP_WINVERSION,
MOZ_APP_VERSION, and MOZ_APP_DISPLAYNAME so the snapshot module.ver still
parses; any other undefined @X@ still fails. The F1-if fixture is rejected
as pepecoin when the upstream parser evaluates `%if 1`.

The makensis -PPO wrapper now also sets installer.nsi's pre-branding
defines (NO_STARTMENU_DIR, NONADMIN_ELEVATE, AbortSurveyURL) after
Unicode true. This is not a full build-environment mirror.
